    <bpmn:process id="W_W5064" name="W5064. LPG HAZMAT Handling, PPE &amp; Emergency-Response Program Design" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Program setup (W5057); HSE policy refresh; incident
Frequency: At setup + periodic refresh + drills
Volume: 1 program × 200 stores + staff
Owner: HSE Manager (VS-24) / Director Store Services
Participants: HSE (VS-24), Store Ops (VS-07), Training (VS-19.4), HR (VS-19), LP/Security (VS-23), BFP/fire consultant
Source: workflow W5064 — LPG HAZMAT Handling, PPE &amp; Emergency-Response Program Design</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5064_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5064_Lane1" name="HSE">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5064_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5064_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5064_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5064_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5064_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5064_Start3" name="Program setup (W5057); HSE policy refresh; incident">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5064_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5064_Task4" name="Define the HAZMAT handling SOP &amp; PPE: cylinder handling/lifting/carry…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Define the HAZMAT handling SOP &amp; PPE: cylinder handling/lifting/carry, no-smoking/ignition control, leak-check, PPE (gloves/eye protection), and the customer safety briefing (links VS-24/VS-147)
Responsible (R): HSE / Store Ops
Accountable (A): HSE Manager
Duration: At setup + refresh</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5064_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5064_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5064_Task5" name="Design the emergency-response plan: leak/fire response, evacuation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Design the emergency-response plan: leak/fire response, evacuation, cylinder-vent procedure, BFP/authority notification, and coordination with VS-26 BC/DR and VS-69 disaster response
Responsible (R): HSE / Security / BFP consultant
Accountable (A): HSE Manager / Director Store Services
Duration: At setup + refresh</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5064_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5064_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5064_Task6" name="Train &amp; drill: certify store staff (VS-19.4 training, links VS-169 PPE)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Train &amp; drill: certify store staff (VS-19.4 training, links VS-169 PPE), conduct leak/fire drills, and refresh on incident lessons (links VS-24/W5075)
Responsible (R): HSE / Training / Store Ops
Accountable (A): HSE Manager
Duration: Initial + periodic drills</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5064_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5064_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5064_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5064_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-755 (ensure controlled execution — LPG Program Strategy, Bulk Supply, Cylinder Fleet &amp; Regulatory Setup (PA-175.1).) | - CTL-755: staff certified before handling (VS-19.4); PPE issued (VS-169); emergency plan tested via drills (VS-24)
Owner: HSE Manager (VS-24) / Director Store Services</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
